## Practical Information

Peloid treatments are available at most spa hotels in Marienbad. A single application lasts 20-30 minutes plus rest time. Treatment is typically administered every other day to allow the body sufficient recovery time. For optimal results, doctors recommend a series of at least 8-10 applications over a period of 2-3 weeks.

Before beginning treatment, a medical examination is conducted. Contraindications include acute inflammation, fever, severe cardiovascular conditions, open wounds and certain skin conditions. Pregnant women should avoid peat treatments.

## Frequently Asked Questions about Peloid Therapy

### What is Marienbad healing peat?

Healing peat is a peloid — a natural remedy from the moorlands of the Slavkovský les (Kaiserwald) forest, distinguished by a particularly high content of humic acids, minerals and organic compounds. It has been used therapeutically in Marienbad for over two centuries.

### What is the difference between a peat pack and a peat bath?

For a peat pack, warm healing peat at 38–42 °C is applied to specific body regions and washed off after 20–30 minutes. A peat bath is a full bath in a peat-and-water suspension at 37–39 °C and is particularly suitable for generalised musculoskeletal complaints and skin conditions.

### Why does peat warmth reach deeper than a hot bath?

Peat has an exceptionally high heat capacity and releases its stored warmth slowly and evenly — the tissue is warmed considerably deeper than in an ordinary hot bath. Added to this is the chemical effect of humic and fulvic acids, which act as anti-inflammatories and antioxidants.

### Which conditions does peloid therapy help with?

Above all musculoskeletal conditions such as osteoarthritis, muscle tension and tendon insertion irritations, as well as skin diseases. The deep warming relieves pain, stimulates circulation and supports lymphatic flow.

### Is peloid therapy suitable for everyone?

No. The spa physician decides on suitability during the initial examination — intensive heat treatments are not appropriate during acute inflammation, for example. Your treatment plan is tailored individually to your state of health.

### Where is peloid therapy offered?

A comprehensive peloid therapy programme with peat packs, peat baths and targeted peat compresses under specialist medical supervision is offered by the Ensana Centrální Lázně in the heart of Marienbad.
